+## Post-Implementation Polish (always, via subagent named in the plan)
+
+After the final whole-branch review is clean but BEFORE deleting the workspace or finishing the branch, **always** run the post-implementation-polish pipeline as a single dispatched subagent. Do NOT run polish inline, do NOT skip it, and do NOT ask the user.
+
+Read the `Polish: post-implementation-polish → <agent type>` line from the plan's `## Agent Assignments` section and dispatch using that agent type. If the plan has no Polish line, fall back to `general-purpose` and note the gap so writing-plans can fix it next time.
+
+The polish subagent owns all six phases (three review rounds, idiomatic pass, /cleanup, strip + humanize comments). It runs them in order, committing between phases, and reports back which phases ran, which were skipped (with reason), commits made, and any unresolved Critical/Important findings. If it surfaces unresolved Critical/Important findings, treat them as a regression: dispatch a fix subagent, then re-run the affected phase. Loop until clean (max 10 iterations across the whole polish stage), then surface to your human partner.
